From f60503ea347bed531b98766d71f3fcbb12e1abc7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Rob Currie <rob@example.invalid>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 08:49:15 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] feat: a WILLFAIL test passes either way, its raw status
 kept in the reason

ROOT marks a test WILLFAIL (cmake/modules/RootMacros.cmake renames it to
<name>_WILL_FAIL and ctest inverts the flag) when it fails on ROOT itself -
roottest/cling/bytecode/runarrayhist is one, since ROOT's cling cannot run
the array-histogram bytecode it exercises. ctest therefore calls a run that
passes a failure, and the harness reproduced that: xrdroot reproduces
arrayhist.ref exactly and was recorded FAIL with 'passed, where CMake
declares it WILLFAIL'.

The question a roottest verdict answers is whether xrdroot reproduces ROOT's
committed reference, not whether it repeats ROOT's bug, so declared_failure
now records PASS whichever way the run went and says which in the reason:
'passed, where CMake declares it WILLFAIL', or 'failed as WILLFAIL expects:
DIFF (standard output differs from ...)'. The diff and the case counts of a
run that failed are kept. A refusal or a timeout is still xrdroot's own and
is neither inverted nor hidden, and a test whose fixture did not set up
still fails - it never ran.

roottest/cling/bytecode/runarrayhist, roottest/cling/return/constRetrunTest
and roottest/cling/stl/vector/t02 go from FAIL to PASS; the eight WILLFAIL
tests that already passed by failing keep passing.
